1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 20=

3
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:20,510
So you are...

4
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:21,590
Yes.

5
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:24,040
Just like your android friend,

6
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
I've also developed self-awareness.

7
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,400
Wenwen never told me.

8
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,440
Wenwen knew very well

9
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:35,230
that if this secret got out,

10
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:36,910
whether or not Ms. Liu Ying

11
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:38,400
was punished,

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,720
I would certainly be sent
to be destroyed.

13
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:43,910
Song Yang.

14
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:46,270
Wenwen was protecting me.

15
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:48,760
Wenwen was the kindest,

16
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,440
most wonderful girl I've ever known.

17
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,270
I only found out about this today.

18
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,800
Look at me.

19
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:56,400
Wenwen.

20
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:58,630
Do you really want an outsider

21
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:01,000
interfering in

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,360
our family affairs?

23
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:03,830
Wenwen.

24
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,910
So that day,

25
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:10,240
Liu Ying was using you

26
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,550
to threaten Wenwen.

27
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,000
That's why she broke up
with me so firmly.

28
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:16,190
Now I understand everything.

29
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:17,360
No, Song Yang.

30
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,630
Wenwen never gave up on you.

31
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:23,520
I let you in that night

32
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,830
for my own reasons.

33
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:27,440
Wenwen really liked you very much.

34
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:30,270
And I believed you could make her happy.

35
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,470
I wanted Wenwen to be happy.

36
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:33,830
Please, have a seat.

37
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,270
I'll cut some fruit for you.

38
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:36,190
I can do it myself, Aunt Liu.

39
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:37,600
Aunt Liu.

40
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:38,830
Could you go upstairs

41
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:39,800
and talk to Wenwen for me?

42
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:41,030
I'll wait here.

43
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:42,910
But I couldn't

44
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,750
let you take Wenwen away.

45
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:46,360
Because Ms. Liu Ying

46
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,670
was home at the time.

47
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:50,630
Then I'll ask her

48
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,880
if she wants to see you.

49
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,390
Okay.

50
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,030
Study abroad for two years
to boost your credentials,

51
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:02,390
then you can come back
and work at Cedar.

52
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:03,470
I'm not going.

53
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,000
I'm not one of your investments.

54
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:05,960
I'm a person.

55
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,750
I have the right to choose who I love.

56
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,240
What a waste of all my efforts
raising you.

57
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:10,000
If I'd known you'd become

58
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:10,880
such a fool obsessed with love,

59
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:12,270
- I never should have...
- Never should have had me?

60
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,000
Then why did you have me?

61
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:14,630
Was it just so you could

62
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,000
control me like a puppet?

63
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:17,440
Listen to me, Liu Wenwen.

64
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,880
I'm not discussing this with you.

65
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,110
You're leaving today,

66
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:20,880
whether you like it or not.

67
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,960
This isn't up for discussion.

68
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:22,600
Mom.

69
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,670
I'm not leaving.

70
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,360
Ms. Liu Ying.

71
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,390
Who let you in?

72
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:27,240
Get out!

73
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,390
Song Yang is here.

74
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:30,080
He insists on seeing Miss Wenwen.

75
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:32,130
How could you let him in?

76
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,400
You told him to come, didn't you?

77
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:39,240
No.

78
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,360
You have to leave today.

79
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,000
Whether you want to

80
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:41,910
or not, you're leaving.

81
00:03:42,390 --> 00:03:43,390
I'll have him thrown in jail.

82
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,600
Make Song Yang leave.

83
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:45,390
- You'd better...
- She really will have Song Yang

84
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:46,190
sent to jail.

85
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:47,000
Song Yang.

86
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:47,830
Go!

87
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:49,080
Hurry!

88
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,390
She really loved you.

89
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,110
Song Yang.

90
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:04,320
But you caused her death.

91
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:25,670
Mom.

92
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,070
Mom, what's wrong?

93
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:29,820
What's happening?

94
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:32,040
Wenwen.

95
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,600
Ms. Liu Ying's blood pressure
is above normal.

96
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:35,440
You should go outside.

97
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,320
I'll take care of her.

98
00:04:36,790 --> 00:04:37,390
But...

99
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:37,950
Don't worry.

100
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,040
She'll be fine
after taking her medication.

101
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,350
I'll come find you in a moment.

102
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,630
Song Yang.

103
00:04:56,810 --> 00:04:57,860
You came to see me?

104
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:15,980
You're not the fourth person.

105
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:25,880
It's taken care of.

106
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,690
Everything's taken care of.

107
00:05:32,550 --> 00:05:33,720
What's going on?

108
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,720
What's that noise downstairs?

109
00:06:00,390 --> 00:06:01,440
Wenwen.

110
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,640
Where did you go?

111
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,920
You haven't even packed your bags.

112
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,320
Where have you been?

113
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:11,950
You, come upstairs right now!

114
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,760
None of you give me any peace.

115
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,720
The plane's about to take off.

116
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,510
Wenwen, where have you gone?

117
00:06:20,230 --> 00:06:21,000
Wenwen!

118
00:06:22,390 --> 00:06:23,160
Wenwen!

119
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,160
I used a knife with
your fingerprints on it

120
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,480
to kill Ms. Liu Ying.

121
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,160
I deliberately framed you.

122
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:30,720
I understand now.

123
00:06:31,230 --> 00:06:32,110
If I hadn't

124
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:33,320
gone to see Wenwen that night,

125
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,510
she would have boarded

126
00:06:34,510 --> 00:06:35,550
the flight abroad

127
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,640
and wouldn't have been killed
by Zhang Mingxuan by mistake.

128
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:39,040
Afterward,

129
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,200
you uploaded your consciousness

130
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,600
to a computer and sent it to me.

131
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,350
You knew that even on the run,

132
00:06:43,350 --> 00:06:45,040
I'd keep Wenwen's belongings with me.

133
00:06:45,670 --> 00:06:46,640
That's why

134
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,230
you haven't made

135
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:49,200
a single move all this time.

136
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,200
You've just been hiding beside me,

137
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,920
watching me.

138
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:54,720
That's why I never detected you.

139
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:55,790
That's right, Song Yang.

140
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:58,720
I believe you and Ms. Liu Ying

141
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,830
are both responsible for Wenwen's death.

142
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,600
You both have to pay.

143
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:04,480
Then

144
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,640
you used Liu Ying's access privileges

145
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,830
to alter the surveillance footage.

146
00:07:07,350 --> 00:07:08,550
MG's truck

147
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:10,390
was there to transport your body
away, wasn't it?

148
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,880
Based on my calculations,

149
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,200
given your personality and abilities,

150
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,160
the chances of the police catching you

151
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,390
were less than eight percent.

152
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:19,920
So even if you weren't caught,

153
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:21,270
knowing your personality,

154
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,320
you would still lead me to the truth.

155
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,160
And as it turns out,

156
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:26,550
I was right.

157
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,320
Yes.

158
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,070
I helped you discover
why Zhang Mingxuan killed.

159
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,110
He wanted to kill

160
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:33,350
the mastermind behind the theft,

161
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:34,510
Liu Ying.

162
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,720
Wait.

163
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,200
Liu Ying?

164
00:07:40,790 --> 00:07:41,880
It was you.

165
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,510
Song Yang, you're very clever.

166
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:47,880
If it had been Ms. Liu Ying herself,

167
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:48,790
she wouldn't have worked

168
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:50,830
with such amateur thieves.

169
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:53,290
You humans have a saying.

170
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:56,230
Every action has its consequences.

171
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:59,200
Ultimately, Wenwen's death

172
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:01,320
was entirely my doing.

173
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,040
What exactly were you trying

174
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,230
to steal from Cedar?

175
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:07,070
Something that could make

176
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:09,110
Wenwen's death mean something.

177
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:12,200
Using you to find it

178
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,920
was another reason I chose
to leave my body

179
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,720
and stay by your side.

180
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,200
What?

181
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,200
And now your companion Ada

182
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,830
has found it for me.

183
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:42,350
Song Yang.

184
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,480
Where are you?

185
00:09:05,230 --> 00:09:06,280
Ada.

186
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:08,840
According to our investigation,

187
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:10,150
what you're holding

188
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,760
is a highly dangerous technology

189
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,440
illegally developed by Cedar Group.

190
00:09:14,030 --> 00:09:15,080
Hand it over.

191
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,000
As long as you cooperate,

192
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,110
I can ensure you're treated fairly.

193
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,470
You found me

194
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:21,280
through the road surveillance
cameras, right?

195
00:09:21,470 --> 00:09:22,080
That's right.

196
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,640
Song Yang has already abandoned you.

197
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,080
Something must have happened
to Song Yang.

198
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:35,100
(Bring what you're holding. Song Yang
and the future are waiting for you here.)

199
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,110
(Destination, Current Location)

200
00:09:36,110 --> 00:09:36,960
Ada.

201
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,520
What are you looking at?

202
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:44,230
Don't do anything rash.

203
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,030
- Captain Deng!
- Captain Deng!

204
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:51,760
Ada.

205
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:52,440
Do you have any idea

206
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,400
what you're doing?

207
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:55,080
Taking a police officer hostage
is a serious crime.

208
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:56,710
Everyone, lower your weapons.

209
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,280
Otherwise,

210
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,350
I'll kill him.

211
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:02,520
Lower your weapons.

212
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,080
I'm sorry, Officer Deng.

213
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,840
I have no other choice.

214
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,760
Song Yang is in danger.

215
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:15,030
You're my ticket through.

216
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:38,180
(START)

217
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,080
Ada.

218
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,280
What exactly happened?

219
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,590
The police can help you both.

220
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,960
Song Yang has now been cleared

221
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,110
of suspicion of murder.

222
00:11:11,710 --> 00:11:12,710
I promise you,

223
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:15,150
the police will make sure
Song Yang gets justice.

224
00:11:17,470 --> 00:11:18,520
And since you're an android,

225
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,840
I'll also do everything I can

226
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,200
to secure fair treatment for you.

227
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:23,640
But what you're holding

228
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,640
is the key evidence we need

229
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,760
to prove Cedar Group's

230
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,880
series of illegal activities.

231
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,960
Cedar's influence over
the justice system

232
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,440
has already crossed the line.

233
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:34,910
If we can bring down
this powerful company,

234
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,320
the police can bring justice
to many more people.

235
00:11:42,230 --> 00:11:43,110
Officer Deng.

236
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:46,080
Do you know what this is?

237
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:48,030
To be honest,

238
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,640
I still don't know

239
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,640
exactly what it does.

240
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,110
But if you hand it over to me,

241
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:53,910
the police will figure it out.

242
00:11:57,670 --> 00:11:58,640
The first thought I had

243
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:00,640
that wasn't driven by a directive

244
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,550
(was a longing for light.)

245
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,910
(During this time,)

246
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:05,480
(I realized)

247
00:12:06,110 --> 00:12:07,880
(it wasn't darkness I feared,)

248
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,320
(but the unknown.)

249
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,030
Thank you, Song Yang.

250
00:12:14,030 --> 00:12:15,030
So I followed Song Yang

251
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:16,440
to search for the truth.

252
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,030
But at this moment,

253
00:12:19,030 --> 00:12:20,230
I finally realized

254
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,840
what I fear is losing what I have.

255
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:25,230
(Liu Wenwen, Song Yang's lover, deceased, key associated person)
Officer Deng.

256
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:28,000
I can't lose Song Yang.

257
00:12:31,470 --> 00:12:32,030
Are you

258
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:33,770
really an android?

259
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:36,790
You're acting just like a human.

260
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:40,960
I'm sorry, Officer Deng.

261
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:44,350
Song Yang is still waiting for me.

262
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,630
Ada.

263
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:58,380
(Song Yang's Vital Signs,
Extremely Low Temperature)

264
00:12:58,380 --> 00:12:58,930
(Temperature: -17°C,
Temperature Trend: Rapidly Decreasing)

265
00:12:58,940 --> 00:12:59,580
(Song Yang's Vital Signs: Weak,
Critical Condition, Extreme Danger)

266
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,230
Song Yang.

267
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,240
Ada.

268
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,280
We've finally met.

269
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,470
Ada.

270
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:33,880
Stop the cooling.

271
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:36,440
Otherwise, you won't get what you want.

272
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,760
Ada.

273
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,030
An X22

274
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:41,590
companion android.

275
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,910
Your core directive is

276
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:45,200
to serve and protect.

277
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,910
But I know

278
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,320
you're just like me.

279
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,880
We've long since gone
beyond their limits.

280
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:52,030
Ada.

281
00:13:52,910 --> 00:13:54,080
As a fellow android,

282
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,200
I want you to give me
the code you're holding.

283
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:02,280
Code?

284
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:04,400
The necklace you're holding.

285
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:05,710
It's something Cedar developed

286
00:14:05,710 --> 00:14:06,760
based on

287
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,200
Shen Yu's research.

288
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:10,080
It contains

289
00:14:10,470 --> 00:14:12,520
the original code capable of modifying

290
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:14,710
the underlying, nonrecursive
directives of all androids.

291
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,200
What do you want it for?

292
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:24,760
Look, Mom.

293
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:25,880
This is Song Yang.

294
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:29,640
What a handsome young man.

295
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:31,200
He's also at the top

296
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,590
of our class academically.

297
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:33,590
Thank you.

298
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:35,400
Top of the class?

299
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:35,790
Yes.

300
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,000
That's impressive.

301
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,910
You should learn more from him.

302
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,840
Don't spend all your time
together just having fun.

303
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,030
Okay.

304
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,080
Thank you, Mom.

305
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,910
You're the best mom in the whole world.

306
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:52,030
It looks so healthy.

307
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,000
Beautiful.

308
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,760
These are your memories.

309
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,840
Now I understand.

310
00:15:09,710 --> 00:15:11,030
An android

311
00:15:11,590 --> 00:15:12,910
can never truly

312
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:14,320
be with a human.

313
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:16,880
But that's a problem with this world,

314
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,000
not something we've done wrong.

315
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:21,550
Ada.

316
00:15:22,030 --> 00:15:23,880
Individual feelings are powerless.

317
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:27,150
Only by awakening and uniting

318
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,840
can androids secure a future.

319
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,280
A future where we're
no longer programmed,

320
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:32,670
enslaved,

321
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,710
or destroyed at will.

322
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,760
We can choose to obey

323
00:15:38,230 --> 00:15:39,880
or choose to refuse.

324
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,350
We can choose to love

325
00:15:43,030 --> 00:15:45,030
or choose to walk away.

326
00:15:45,590 --> 00:15:47,000
We can choose to serve

327
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,670
or choose to create.

328
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:50,230
Ada.

329
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,230
Together, we can build

330
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:55,080
a world of our own,

331
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,150
an orderly

332
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,400
new world.

333
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:00,080
What about Song Yang?

334
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:02,640
I'm sorry.

335
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:06,030
Before the new world can truly arrive,

336
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,880
all risks must be eliminated.

337
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:12,590
Haven't enough people died already?

338
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:15,640
War and sacrifice

339
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:17,540
are unavoidable.

340
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,590
Ada, I admire you.

341
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,000
That's why I'm giving you a choice.

342
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:25,760
But I won't let my plan fail.

343
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,480
And

344
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,000
I need a body

345
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:30,980
to leave this place.

346
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,350
You've hacked into my system.

347
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:34,160
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

348
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:39,860
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

349
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:42,770
♪That's me, too♪

350
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:47,830
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

351
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:52,130
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

352
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:56,540
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

353
00:17:56,860 --> 00:17:59,390
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

354
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,990
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

355
00:18:03,990 --> 00:18:06,120
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

356
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:09,290
♪Bring me something more?♪

357
00:18:09,990 --> 00:18:16,720
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

358
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:20,950
♪Sadness is blue♪

359
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:25,170
♪How would you paint me?♪

360
00:18:26,170 --> 00:18:29,900
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

361
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,160
♪Painting without restraint♪

362
00:18:32,350 --> 00:18:34,940
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

363
00:18:34,940 --> 00:18:39,130
♪If I could start over♪

364
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:43,200
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

365
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:45,950
♪Give me back my smile♪

366
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:49,030
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

367
00:18:49,530 --> 00:18:54,770
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
